Priya,

Confirmed on the debit/ATM side. Debit card and ATM claims of $250 or less ar=
e automatically provisionally credited by ClaimTrack 2.0 on the first busines=
s day after the claim is opened.

I am not seeing a manual exception route for standard debit/ATM claims in CPS=
-SOP-211 or JA-114. The only practical holds we are applying today are operat=
ional:
- claim not yet classified as eligible debit/ATM
- duplicate/repeat claim in ClaimTrack
- active fraud referral or other system stop
- high-value review routed under CPS-SOP-219

If someone is asking whether the analyst can suppress the auto-credit for a l=
ow-dollar claim just because the customer is =E2=80=9Cnot really a dispute pe=
rson,=E2=80=9D I would say no. The system does it once the claim is opened an=
d coded correctly in ClaimTrack 2.0.

